From 822b017d2bf31f72f85981ae6680d3b79e0f532d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Damien Dusha <Damien Dusha>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:52:49 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] lwIP NSD: make the shutdown branch reachable, and release the
 core lock in it

unreg_task_ptp() asks the NSD to shut down with {-1, -1} in two enum fields.
Both enums are non-negative, so on a short-enum ABI (arm-none-eabi GCC's
default, Tag_ABI_enum_size: small) they are unsigned bytes holding 255 and
`init->tp == -1` is always false: GCC deletes the branch. Where enums are
int-sized the branch is live, and it returns with LOCK_TCPIP_CORE() still
held, which stops the whole lwIP stack.

Compare against the enum's own -1, and unlock before returning.

Measured on a NUCLEO-H563ZI (FreeRTOS + lwIP, core locking on), stopping PTP
via unreg_task_ptp() and pinging the board:

    upstream                 branch compiled out; stack survives by accident
    comparison fixed only    branch live; stack dead after stop (100% loss)
    this fix                 two stop/start cycles, 0% loss, PTP resyncs

nsd_etherlib.c and nsd_linux.c compare the same sentinel the same way; not
changed here because they cannot be tested from this project.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../port/example_netstack_drivers/nsd_lwip.c     | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/flexptp/port/example_netstack_drivers/nsd_lwip.c b/src/flexptp/port/example_netstack_drivers/nsd_lwip.c
index d280f2b..a06e43c 100644
--- a/src/flexptp/port/example_netstack_drivers/nsd_lwip.c
+++ b/src/flexptp/port/example_netstack_drivers/nsd_lwip.c
@@ -75,10 +75,24 @@ void ptp_nsd_init(const NsdInitSettings * init) {
     }
 
     // calling either parameter with -1 just closes connections
-    if ((init->tp == -1) || (init->dm == -1)) {
+    //
+    // Compared as the ENUM's -1, not the int's. unreg_task_ptp() passes {-1, -1}, which is
+    // stored into PtpTransportType/PtpDelayMechanism fields; both enums are non-negative, so on a
+    // short-enum ABI -- arm-none-eabi GCC's default -- they are unsigned bytes, the -1 is stored
+    // as 255, and `init->tp == -1` is always false. GCC then deletes this branch outright and a
+    // shutdown request falls through as a "transport 255" reconfiguration instead. Casting the
+    // constant to the field's type makes the comparison mean the same thing on every ABI.
+    if ((init->tp == (PtpTransportType)-1) || (init->dm == (PtpDelayMechanism)-1)) {
         // message transmission and reception is turned off
         TP = -1;
         DM = -1;
+
+        // Release the core lock taken above. This early return used to leave it held: with
+        // LWIP_TCPIP_CORE_LOCKING the core mutex then stays owned by a thread that has moved on,
+        // and the whole stack stops, not just PTP -- ARP, ICMP and every other UDP/TCP user block
+        // on the next LOCK_TCPIP_CORE() for ever. Wherever the branch above is live (int-sized
+        // enums, or short ones once the comparison is fixed), unreg_task_ptp() comes through here.
+        UNLOCK_TCPIP_CORE();
         return;
     }
 
